{"base_rate":0.31357048748353095,"brier":0.11398511198945982,"bss":0.4704377707704962,"bss_hi":0.5496982924348452,"bss_lo":0.378147117687996,"country":"AU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08383399209486164,"ess":256.9734835416607,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Perth</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Perth rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>89%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 759 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nPERTH METRO, 3.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.47, ranked 17 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(6&ndash;41) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>455</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>155</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 4 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Perth</b> <span class=\"muted\">AU</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.47</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>6&ndash;41\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>759 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Perth &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Perth\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.610505494505496,378.0 145.86958904109588,257.3424657534247 309.8523684210527,89.84210526315786 408.5970322580645,18.0 408.5970322580645,27.393548387096757 309.8523684210527,156.89473684210526 145.86958904109588,322.16438356164383 59.610505494505496,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"267.86034255599475\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"267.86034255599475\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.610505494505496,350.8 145.86958904109588,302.2191780821918 309.8523684210527,166.47368421052633 408.5970322580645,57.92258064516125\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 455 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.610505494505496\" cy=\"350.8\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"145.86958904109588\" cy=\"302.2191780821918\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 71%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"309.8523684210527\" cy=\"166.47368421052633\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 155 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"408.5970322580645\" cy=\"57.92258064516125\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(31%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Perth the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.48) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.24).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.239</td><td class='num'>12.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'>0.333</td><td class='num'>1.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>183</td><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'>0.377</td><td class='num'>12.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'>0.479</td><td class='num'>6.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-31.95224,"lon":115.8614,"n":759,"n_cities":109,"name":"Perth","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.09800000000000068,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00454945054945055,"n":455,"obs":0.08571428571428572,"sig":true},{"hi":0.51,"lo":0.09800000000000068,"mean":0.2482191780821918,"n":73,"obs":0.2191780821917808,"sig":false},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.51,"mean":0.7114473684210527,"n":76,"obs":0.5921052631578947,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.9903870967741935,"n":155,"obs":0.8903225806451613,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.8,"rank":17,"rank_hi":41.0,"rank_lo":6.0,"reliability":0.007501209520188621,"resolution":0.10768008354147929,"slug":"perth","station":"PERTH METRO","timezone":"Australia/Perth"}